---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import WaitlistForm from "../components/WaitlistForm.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Porphyra"
  description="Score every job posting before you apply. Porphyra reads the JD against your CV, tells you honestly whether it's worth your time, and keeps your CV and reports encrypted — the server never reads them unless you ask it to."
>
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">For job seekers everywhere — most of you remote</p>
      <h1>Fewer applications. Better ones.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Porphyra reads a job posting against your CV and gives you a scored, honest read
        before you spend an evening tailoring anything — including telling you when a role
        isn't worth applying to.
      </p>
      <div id="waitlist">
        <WaitlistForm />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="problem">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2>Applying to everything is the same as applying to nothing</h2>
        <p>
          The average listing gets hundreds of applications within days. Sending fifty
          generic ones doesn't beat that math — it just spends fifty evenings to lose fifty
          times instead of once. Recruiters can tell. So can the ATS keyword filter before a
          human ever opens your CV.
        </p>
        <p>
          Porphyra starts from the opposite premise: read the posting properly, score it
          honestly against what you actually bring, and only spend real effort — tailored
          CV, cover letter, outreach — on the roles that clear the bar.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mechanism">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2>How it works</h2>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>
            <span class="step-num">1</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Paste a posting</h3>
              <p>A URL or the raw text. Porphyra reads the full description, not just the title.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="step-num">2</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Get a scored, six-dimension read</h3>
              <p>
                Profile match, target alignment, compensation, cultural signals, red flags,
                and growth trajectory — plus a check for whether the posting looks like it's
                actually still open.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="step-num">3</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Below 4.0? We say so</h3>
              <p>
                Porphyra actively recommends against applying to weak matches instead of
                staying quiet about it. You always make the final call.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="step-num">4</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Track it, or don't apply at all</h3>
              <p>
                Strong matches move into a pipeline with real states — evaluated, applied,
                interview, offer — so you know where every application actually stands.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="security-teaser">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2>Your CV isn't the server's business until you say so</h2>
        <p>
          Your CV, evaluation reports and notes are encrypted in your browser before they
          ever reach us — we store ciphertext we can't read. When you ask for an evaluation,
          your CV and the job description are decrypted for that one request, sent to the AI
          provider, and the result is re-encrypted before it's saved. We built the honest
          version of "we take security seriously": a page that says exactly what's encrypted,
          what isn't, and why.
        </p>
        <a class="link-arrow" href="/security">Read the full security model &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pricing-teaser">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2>Start free. Upgrade when it's paying for itself.</h2>
        <p>
          A free tier that's actually useful for a real search, and one paid plan when you
          want more evaluations and CV tailoring. No enterprise sales call.
        </p>
        <a class="link-arrow" href="/pricing">See pricing &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="final-cta">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2>Get early access</h2>
        <p>We're building in the open. Join the list and we'll email you when it's ready.</p>
        <WaitlistForm />
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--p-space-24) var(--p-space-6) var(--p-space-16);
    text-align: center;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-size: var(--p-text-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-brand-text);
    margin: 0;
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--p-font-display);
    font-size: var(--p-text-6xl);
    line-height: var(--p-leading-tight);
    margin: var(--p-space-4) 0;
    color: var(--p-porphyra-900);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--p-text-xl);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin: 0 auto;
    max-width: 36rem;
  }

  .section-inner {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--p-space-16) var(--p-space-6);
  }
  .problem,
  .pricing-teaser {
    background: var(--color-surface-sunken);
  }
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--p-font-display);
    font-size: var(--p-text-3xl);
    color: var(--p-porphyra-900);
    margin: 0 0 var(--p-space-4);
  }
  .problem p,
  .security-teaser p,
  .pricing-teaser p,
  .final-cta p {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: var(--p-text-lg);
  }

  .steps {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--p-space-8);
  }
  .steps li {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--p-space-4);
  }
  .step-num {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 2.25rem;
    height: 2.25rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-brand-soft);
    color: var(--color-brand-text);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .steps h3 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--p-space-1);
    font-size: var(--p-text-lg);
  }
  .steps p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .link-arrow {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: var(--p-space-2);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .final-cta {
    text-align: center;
  }
</style>
